The revised local gates now pass G1–G8. At the shipping candidate (`n=127`), the exact answer space is \(2^{127}\) with one valid witness, all five construction-aware attacks fail 0/8, DPLL succeeds as expected in about 10,956 literal inspections, Gaussian elimination uses about 155,060 scalar bit operations, and the fully counted compact arithmetic route is 223 operations. I’m moving to the mandatory bare oracle run; this may still hit the OpenRouter account-limit error already recorded in the workspace.
STEP 0 supports a Track B family via Theorem 1. The module has been revised so the compact-route operation count is honest and its block grouping is public.
