codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator using the paper’s Theorem 1 3-SAT-to-PAFP reduction. The full paper was reviewed, including its polynomial easy regimes. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/html/1111.3996v3)

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1111.3996/gen_1111_3996.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1111.3996/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1111.3996/README.md)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1111.3996/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1111.3996/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1111.3996/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Results:

- G1–G8 pass.
- Exact answer density: \(2^{-127}\); sampled guesses: 0/200,000.
- Five attacks each failed 0/8.
- Disclosed Gaussian reference: 155,060 mean scalar-bit operations.
- Compact route: 223 exact operations.
- G9 size/effort caps pass.

The result is not yet releasable: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” for every bare, hinted, and placebo attempt. Consequently G9 remains correctly false and `selftest_report.json` has `"pass": false`. No hardness verdict was fabricated, and the paper was not rejected.
